Q: Disable Computers with Powershell A: <p>I know this is an old post but I believe it's a type mismatch of Disable-ADAccount expecting a property rather than the whole object for input.</p>
<p>Using the example I added .DistinguishedName to the item passed to Disable-ADAccount and it worked. The input csv would need to have DistinguishedName available to the command though.</p>
<pre><code>{
Disable-ADAccount $StaleComputer.DistinguishedName
Move-ADObject $StaleComputer.DistinguishedName -TargetPath &quot;OU=Disabled Computers, DC=domain, DC=com&quot;
}
</code></pre>

Q: Laravel :Failed to authenticate on SMTP server with username using 2 possible authenticators A: <p>Sorry, I know this is an old thread but i came across a similar issue with <strong>GoDaddy SMTP</strong> with the <strong>Laravel</strong> application running on <strong>AWS EC2</strong>. The below code works for me maybe it will help you guys too.</p>
<pre><code>MAIL_DRIVER=smtp
MAIL_HOST=&quot;relay-hosting.secureserver.net&quot;
MAIL_PORT=25
MAIL_USERNAME=&quot;&lt;your_email@example.com&gt;&quot;
MAIL_PASSWORD=&quot;&lt;your_password&gt;&quot;
MAIL_ENCRYPTION=tls
MAIL_FROM_NAME=&quot;${APP_NAME}&quot;
MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=&quot;&lt;your_email@example.com&gt;&quot;
</code></pre>

